From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hfp: leave SCO requests alone with ENABLE_HFP_DECLINE_SCO

Not from upstream. The CYW43439's Bluetooth firmware on Pico W boards
accepts a synchronous connection and never completes it, and the ACL
link to the phone then drops with a supervision timeout
(raspberrypi/pico-sdk#1461). HFP answers a SCO or eSCO request from its
HCI event handler, ahead of the host's connection filter, so a filter
alone can't decline it. With ENABLE_HFP_DECLINE_SCO, HFP leaves the
request to the filter, and the call's audio stays on the phone.

--- a/src/classic/hfp.c
+++ b/src/classic/hfp.c
@@ -875,6 +875,10 @@
             switch(hci_event_connection_request_get_link_type(packet)){
                 case 0: //  SCO
                 case 2: // eSCO
+#ifdef ENABLE_HFP_DECLINE_SCO
+                    // the controller can't carry SCO: leave the request to the connection filter, which declines it
+                    break;
+#endif
                     hci_event_connection_request_get_bd_addr(packet, event_addr);
                     hfp_connection = get_hfp_connection_context_for_bd_addr(event_addr, local_role);
                     if (!hfp_connection) break;
